{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"894ecdc0644bf72e","type":"text","text":"# **New Homework** \n### - **Study Grammar 4 and Grammar 5 and finish the remaining E exercises.**","x":-325,"y":62,"width":650,"height":172,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"5b1c8d9aa4e9ab65","type":"text","text":"\n## **13:35** -\tGrammar E\n## **13:50** -\tGrammar E Exercises \n## **14:20** -   Homework for next week\n\n","x":-324,"y":-133,"width":649,"height":156,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"de2d86d4382775e0","type":"text","text":"# **Today's Class: Writing and Grammar**","x":-301,"y":-234,"width":602,"height":68,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"41f47054a6649ba9","type":"text","text":"## How do we form the Past Perfect?\n\nGRAMMAR FORMULA\n\n## Subject + had + past participle \n\nWe use had with every subject.\n\n|Subject|Had|Past participle|\n|---|---|---|\n|I|had|eaten|\n|You|had|finished|\n|He / She / It|had|gone|\n|We|had|studied|\n|They|had|arrived|\n\n### Positive sentences (+)\n\n- I had eaten breakfast before school.\n    \n- She had finished her test before the bell rang.\n    \n- They had left when we arrived.\n    \n- We had studied English before the exam.\n    \n\n### Negative sentences (-)\n\nSubject + had not + past participle\n\nWe can shorten had not to hadn't.\n\n- I hadn't finished my homework.\n    \n- She hadn't eaten breakfast before school.\n    \n- They hadn't seen the film before.\n    \n- We hadn't studied enough before the exam.\n    \n\n### Questions (?)\n\nHad + subject + past participle?\n\n- Had you finished your homework?\n    \n- Had she already left?\n    \n- Had they eaten before the party?\n    \n- Had he studied for the test?","x":1559,"y":645,"width":440,"height":1207,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"296f1c6042a9cb9b","type":"text","text":"### Compare\n\nPast Simple:\n\n\"I finished my homework at 6 o'clock.\"\n\nThis tells us about one completed action in the past.\n\nPast Perfect:\n\n\"I had finished my homework before my friend arrived.\"\n\nThis tells us that the homework was already finished when my friend arrived.","x":1376,"y":-200,"width":616,"height":412,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"5b90763dea1b4424","type":"text","text":"## What is a past participle?\n\nA past participle is the third form of a verb, also called V3.\n\nRegular verbs usually end in -ed.\n\n|Base verb (V1)|Past Simple (V2)|Past participle (V3)|\n|---|---|---|\n|work|worked|worked|\n|play|played|played|\n|finish|finished|finished|\n|study|studied|studied|\n|clean|cleaned|cleaned|\n|eat|ate|eaten|\n|go|went|gone|\n|see|saw|seen|\n|write|wrote|written|\n|do|did|done|\n|take|took|taken|\n|forget|forgot|forgotten|\n|leave|left|left|\n|buy|bought|bought|\n\nImportant: Always use the past participle after had.\n\nIncorrect: She had went home.\n\nCorrect: She had gone home.\n\nIncorrect: They had ate dinner.\n\nCorrect: They had eaten dinner.","x":749,"y":809,"width":471,"height":952,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"87cf5077457c531b","type":"text","text":"### Use had + past participle.\n\n1. She __________ (finish) her homework before dinner.\n    \n2. They __________ (leave) when we arrived.\n    \n3. I __________ (eat) breakfast before I went to school.\n    \n4. He __________ (forget) his password.\n    \n5. We __________ (see) that film before.\n    \n6. My brother __________ (break) his phone.\n    \n7. The teacher __________ (start) the lesson before I arrived.\n    \n8. Sarah __________ (write) the email before lunchtime.","x":215,"y":809,"width":488,"height":609,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"765278f548069f57","type":"text","text":"## Make the sentences negative\n\nExample:\n\nI had finished my work.\n\nI hadn't finished my work.\n\n1. She had eaten lunch.\n    \n2. They had studied for the exam.\n    \n3. He had cleaned his room.\n    \n4. We had seen the film.\n    \n5. Tom had done his homework.","x":215,"y":1488,"width":412,"height":333,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"3ce783e2765d54ab","type":"text","text":"\n## Prepositions of time\n\nFill in the gaps with IN, ON or AT.\n\n1. I wake up ___ 7 o'clock.\n    \n2. My birthday is ___ August.\n    \n3. We have English ___ Monday.\n    \n4. I was born ___ 2011.\n    \n5. The film starts ___ 8:30.\n    \n6. We go skiing ___ winter.\n    \n7. My exam is ___ Friday morning.\n    \n8. I study ___ the evening.\n    \n9. My parents sometimes work ___ night.\n    \n10. We visit our grandparents ___ Christmas Day.\n    \n11. I have football practice ___ Thursday.\n    \n12. Our holiday is ___ July.","x":3589,"y":2702,"width":454,"height":791,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"26f74dd7c12f9fa0","type":"text","text":"## Prepositions of place\n\nFill in the gaps with IN, ON or AT.\n\n1. My books are ___ my schoolbag.\n    \n2. The clock is ___ the wall.\n    \n3. We are waiting ___ the bus stop.\n    \n4. She lives ___ Utrecht.\n    \n5. My phone is ___ the table.\n    \n6. He is ___ home.\n    \n7. The students are ___ the classroom.\n    \n8. There is some juice ___ the fridge.\n    \n9. My sister is ___ the train.\n    \n10. My dad is ___ work.\n    \n11. The picture is ___ the wall.\n    \n12. We are meeting ___ the station.","x":4145,"y":2702,"width":370,"height":754,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"42c57298ea7ba040","type":"text","text":"## MIXED GRAMMAR \nComplete the sentences using the correct tense or preposition.\n\n1. I __________ (finish) my homework before my friend arrived.\n    \n2. The lesson starts ___ 8:30.\n    \n3. My keys are ___ my bag.\n    \n4. She __________ (leave) before the teacher came.\n    \n5. We have a maths test ___ Wednesday.\n    \n6. The books are ___ the shelf.\n    \n7. Tom was tired because he __________ (not sleep) well.\n    \n8. I was born ___ 2012.\n    \n9. When I arrived at the cinema, the film __________ (already start).\n    \n10. My brother is waiting ___ the bus stop.","x":4579,"y":2702,"width":422,"height":810,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"a6e1dbd5777214d0","type":"text","text":"# THE PAST PERFECT\n\n## 1. What is the Past Perfect?\n\nWe use the Past Perfect to talk about an action that happened before another action or moment in the past.\n\nWhen we talk about two things that happened in the past, the Past Perfect helps us understand which action happened first.\n\nExample:\n\nI had finished my homework before my mum came home.\n\nTwo things happened:\n\n- First: I finished my homework.\n    \n- Second: My mum came home.\n    \n\nThe first action uses the Past Perfect:\n\nhad finished\n\nThe second action uses the Past Simple:\n\ncame","x":497,"y":-231,"width":793,"height":757,"color":"3"}
	],
